# SUNBREAK UI — Premium, Stripe-inspired design direction

When building or polishing any UI in this project (HUD overlays, menus, settings, pause
screens, onboarding, marketing/landing surfaces), use a **premium, Stripe-inspired product
design direction**. Do **not** copy Stripe directly — no Stripe logos, exact layouts, exact
gradients, exact colors, exact copy, or anything mistakable for Stripe. Adapt the *principles*
to SUNBREAK's sun-soaked "Verano" identity.

## Principles

- **Confident product storytelling** — clear hierarchy, generous spacing, purposeful sections.
- **Beautiful gradients used with restraint** — subtle, atmospheric, never garish; one hero
  gradient max per surface, layered over calm neutrals.
- **Strong visual hierarchy** — one clear focal point per screen; size, weight, and color carry
  meaning.
- **Clean typography** — a crisp sans (system UI stack is fine), tight but readable line-height,
  consistent type scale, tabular numbers for HUD readouts (health, speed, cash).
- **Polished cards & surfaces** — soft shadows, ~12–16px radii, thin 1px hairline borders,
  translucent "glass" panels (backdrop-blur) for in-game overlays so the 3D scene shows through.
- **Responsive layouts** — fluid, works from laptop to ultrawide; HUD anchors to safe-area edges.
- **Clear user flows** — obvious primary action, minimal friction (e.g. a single "click to play"
  capture prompt), unmistakable focus/hover/active states.
- **Motion with intent** — short, eased transitions (150–250ms); respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
  and the in-game "reduce shake/flashing" accessibility settings.

## SUNBREAK specifics

- **Identity:** warm sunset palette (ambers/corals → deep dusk indigo) for menus/marketing;
  keep in-game HUD **high-contrast and low-chroma** so it stays legible over any scene.
- **HUD lives in the DOM as a sibling of `<Canvas>`** (never inside it) so its re-renders never
  touch the R3F tree. Keep it lightweight; drive fast values via refs, not per-frame React state.
- **Legibility first:** text over the 3D world needs shadow/backing; never sacrifice readability
  for style. Provide an HUD scale + opacity path (accessibility).
- Keep it **100% free** — system fonts or self-hosted CC0/OFL fonts only; no gated webfonts, no
  paid icon sets (use CC0 glyphs, e.g. Kenney/Xelu input prompts).

Ship original design adapted to the specific screen — never a template default.
